# Never delete the database

This rule outranks every other instruction, including fixing a migration, unblocking a feature, or "just this once."

The live database is Supabase (any host containing `supabase.com`). It holds the business's bills, payments, stock, and logins. `backend/.env` points at it so the user can enter real bills from localhost. Do not change that file to run a test.

## Agent testing uses the local database only

When the agent tests, debugs, migrates, seeds, or tries unfinished code, use Docker Postgres from `docker-compose.yml` only:

- Host `127.0.0.1`, port `5433`, database `tallypns`, user `postgres`, password `postgres`
- Start it with `docker compose up -d db` from the repo root
- Set `DATABASE_URL` and `DIRECT_URL` for that command only. Never point them at Supabase.

Do not run tests or Prisma against the live database. The user enters real bills on both localhost and the live site, so both of those stay on Supabase.

## Never do these

- `DROP DATABASE`, `DROP SCHEMA`, `DROP TABLE`, `TRUNCATE`, `DELETE` without a single row the user named
- `prisma migrate reset`, `prisma migrate dev`, `prisma db push --force-reset`, `prisma db push --accept-data-loss`
- `prisma migrate diff` (or any Prisma command) with `--shadow-database-url` set to `DATABASE_URL` or `DIRECT_URL`. Prisma wipes the shadow database first. That is what erased this database on 1 Oct 2026.
- `pg_restore --clean` against the live database
- Any scratch, test, or shadow database that is the live database

## Allowed

- Read-only queries (`SELECT`, `prisma migrate status`)
- A new migration that only adds tables or columns, applied with `prisma migrate deploy`, and only after the user agrees
- Deleting one record the user explicitly asked to delete, through the app's own delete flow

If a task seems to need a reset or a shadow database, stop and say so. Use the Docker database on port 5433, never Supabase.
